# A colossus's foot comes down fifty kilometres off and the player FEELS it
# (src/systems/19_colossi.gd). The looming walker is staged seven world minutes
# before its leg lands; the ground brings the landing at 3 km/s, so about
# seventeen real seconds later the view sways (a quake, CameraRig.quake) and the
# footfall sounds, and the boom comes through the air two and a half minutes
# after that. Frames a quarter of a second apart while the ground moves show the
# picture swaying and settling; the awaits prove each arrives, in order, at its
# own speed.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/colossi_step.tour --seed=7 --place=coast --hour=12 --colossus=1@728 --view=shoulder --face=314 --weather=clear:0
wait 3
shot 00-before-it-lands with land:coast
await colossus_quake 40
shot 01-the-ground-moves with land:coast
wait 0.25
shot 02-sway with land:coast
wait 0.25
shot 03-sway with land:coast
wait 0.25
shot 04-sway with land:coast
await sound:colossus_step 5
wait 4
shot 05-settled with land:coast
await sound:colossus_boom 180
shot 06-the-boom-arrives with land:coast
